WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:19.351
"Gliss doesn't seem very excited about the expedition," Zann said to Boz the next day.

2
00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:22.127
They were at Teplo's house, preparing to depart.

3
00:00:22.128 --> 00:00:24.869
"Why are her parents making her go?"

4
00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:29.722
"Her uncle Gar is an important member of the expedition," Boz said.

5
00:00:29.723 --> 00:00:35.057
"Gliss' parents thought this would be a good educational opportunity for her."

6
00:00:35.058 --> 00:00:40.822
Zann didn't believe it. He wondered if Gliss' parents were trying to push her and Zann together again.

7
00:00:40.823 --> 00:00:45.218
They probably weren't happy that she had become so close to Darb, a Void.

8
00:00:45.219 --> 00:00:51.553
Teplo rushed in, his goose snapping irritably at his heels. "Ready to go?" Teplo asked.

9
00:00:51.554 --> 00:00:55.629
"Ready." Boz grabbed Zann by the elbow and snapped his fingers.

10
00:00:55.630 --> 00:01:00.083
Zann barely had time to grab Zing before his grandfather zapped them away.

11
00:01:00.084 --> 00:01:07.299
They landed on a grassy lawn, in front of an ancient stone mansion. Beyond was deep forest.

12
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:10.742
"Where are we?" Zann spotted a large ship.

13
00:01:10.743 --> 00:01:17.104
A heap of colorful fabric was attached to it by a number of heavy ropes. "And what's that?"

14
00:01:17.105 --> 00:01:22.451
"This place is called Moonstone Manor," Teplo said, appearing beside them.

15
00:01:22.452 --> 00:01:27.169
"And that's the airship that will transport us to the Cave."

16
00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:34.421
Zann was surprised. "I know people can't just zap to the Cave of the Unknown because of its weird energy—"

17
00:01:34.422 --> 00:01:43.585
"Correct," Teplo interrupted. "The Cave, as well as the relics inside, constantly sends out destabilizing surges.

18
00:01:43.586 --> 00:01:47.953
It makes performing any magic near the Cave very dangerous."

19
00:01:47.954 --> 00:01:52.228
"But I didn't know there was a special airship," Zann continued.

20
00:01:52.229 --> 00:01:55.788
"I assumed we'd fly there on dragons or something."

21
00:01:55.789 --> 00:02:01.163
"The Cave's unstable energy frightens most creatures," someone said.

22
00:02:01.164 --> 00:02:07.961
It was Venna. "Even the best-trained riding dragons usually refuse to fly anywhere near it."

23
00:02:07.962 --> 00:02:11.305
Venna was representing the Red Council on the expedition.

24
00:02:11.306 --> 00:02:14.091
Beside her was a tall, handsome man.

25
00:02:14.092 --> 00:02:18.792
Venna introduced him as Tok, the airship's pilot. She turned to Zann.

26
00:02:18.793 --> 00:02:27.016
"This vehicle is the traditional way of traveling to the Cave of the Unknown," she said. "Come inside and have a look."

27
00:02:27.017 --> 00:02:30.274
The airship's main room looked like someone's living room.

28
00:02:30.275 --> 00:02:33.202
Tok led the way down a hallway and into another room.

29
00:02:33.203 --> 00:02:39.854
Three large, vicious-looking creatures with fiery red scales were writhing in a tank of thick glass.

30
00:02:39.855 --> 00:02:44.094
When Zann and the others entered, the creatures spit balls of flame at them.

31
00:02:44.095 --> 00:02:47.585
Zann jumped back, and Zing cowered behind him.

32
00:02:47.586 --> 00:02:50.237
But the flames didn't penetrate the glass wall.

33
00:02:50.238 --> 00:02:55.553
"Are those dragons?" Zann asked. "I've never seen any like that!"

34
00:02:55.554 --> 00:02:59.431
"They're known as flame furies," Teplo explained.

35
00:02:59.432 --> 00:03:02.468
"They originally came from another world."

36
00:03:02.469 --> 00:03:09.311
"And many years ago," said Boz, "several young furies were smuggled into Magica.

37
00:03:09.312 --> 00:03:19.145
They've been breeding in the darkest reaches of the forest beyond Mount Mystery ever since. Few people know they exist."

38
00:03:19.146 --> 00:03:28.531
Venna nodded. "The original owner of this manor caught these three furies and found a way to harness their fiery power to travel to the Cave."

39
00:03:28.532 --> 00:03:33.666
She swept a hand at the vehicle. "He called it the Dragon Wagon."

40
00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:38.940
Zann stared at the fierce creatures. He wished Darb could be there to see them.

41
00:03:38.941 --> 00:03:42.303
Darb loved learning about new magical creatures!

42
00:03:42.304 --> 00:03:50.320
"When we're ready to go," Tok explained, "we'll release an image of the snuffer, which is the furies' natural enemy from their home world.

43
00:03:50.321 --> 00:03:54.800
The furies will blast it with their flaming breath until the image is removed."

44
00:03:54.801 --> 00:04:00.769
"Or until the image is so singed that the furies realize it's not real," Teplo said.

45
00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:06.963
"Indeed." Tok chuckled. "We have to replace the fake snuffer for each journey."

46
00:04:06.964 --> 00:04:11.387
Zann wondered what kind of terrifying creature could scare the furies.

47
00:04:11.388 --> 00:04:16.056
Before he could ask, several other people entered, including Gliss and her uncle.

48
00:04:16.057 --> 00:04:23.165
Uncle Gar greeted everyone cheerfully, but Gliss looked glum. Zann could tell she wasn't thrilled to be there.

49
00:04:23.166 --> 00:04:27.749
"Let's get started," said Venna. "We have a long journey ahead."

50
00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:32.132
Tok nodded. "Snuffer up."

51
00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:37.630
A metal sculpture popped into view at the back of the furies' tank.

52
00:04:37.631 --> 00:04:44.603
"That's a snuffer?" Zann exclaimed. "There's one of those on my parents' storage shelf at the lab!"

53
00:04:44.604 --> 00:04:56.375
"That makes sense," Teplo said. "Their last journey was to the Cave. Well, second-to-last."

54
00:04:56.376 --> 00:05:01.698
The airship shuddered and lifted. "You should go sit down," Tok said to the group.

55
00:05:01.699 --> 00:05:06.166
"It can be tricky keeping your balance when the airship takes off."

56
00:05:06.167 --> 00:05:10.722
The furies' fiery breath quickly filled the Dragon Wagon's cloth balloon.

57
00:05:10.723 --> 00:05:17.235
Soon the airship was flying over the treetops.

58
00:05:17.236 --> 00:05:20.755
Zann spent the first hour of the journey peering out the window.

59
00:05:20.756 --> 00:05:29.159
Then Gliss' uncle called Zann's name. "You kids don't have to sit here with us boring old people," he said with a wink.

60
00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:32.897
"Why don't you two explore the rest of the ship together?"

61
00:05:32.898 --> 00:05:41.468
Zann forced a smile. He didn't want the adults to know that he and Gliss weren't on good terms. "Sure. Let's go, Gliss."

62
00:05:41.469 --> 00:05:44.547
They headed into the hallway leading to the furies' tank.

63
00:05:44.548 --> 00:05:48.480
"Are you still mad at me?" Gliss asked tentatively.

64
00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:52.471
"You know how important finding my parents is to me."

65
00:05:52.472 --> 00:05:55.952
He glared at her. "At least you should know."

66
00:05:55.953 --> 00:05:57.930
"Zann—" Gliss began.

67
00:05:57.931 --> 00:06:02.288
Zing interrupted her with an excited squawk. The little dragon rushed forward.

68
00:06:02.289 --> 00:06:07.815
"Zing, leave the furies alone," Zann said. "They'll roast you alive!"

69
00:06:07.816 --> 00:06:10.102
But Zing wasn't heading for the tank.

70
00:06:10.103 --> 00:06:12.925
He was scratching at a large feed bin.

71
00:06:12.926 --> 00:06:20.166
The expedition leaders had packed plenty of food for humans and dragons alike, since it was risky to conjure anything near the Cave.

72
00:06:20.167 --> 00:06:22.606
"Is he hungry?" Gliss wondered.

73
00:06:22.607 --> 00:06:28.057
Zann hurried over to the bin. "I guess Tok wouldn't mind if Zing had a snack."

74
00:06:28.058 --> 00:06:31.632
He swung open the top and gasped in shock.

75
00:06:31.633 --> 00:06:34.452
Perda and Darb were crouched inside!

76
00:06:34.453 --> 00:06:41.780
"Surprise!" Perda stood up. "We didn't want to miss all the fun!"
